Object Pool Design Pattern -
The Object Pool Design Pattern is a creational pattern that manages a pool of reusable objects instead of creating and destroying them repeatedly.
👉 Instead of new every time, you borrow an object from the pool and return it after use.

ObjectPool design pattern is used with singleton design pattern and require thread safety while acquiring and releasing
the lock.

🧠 Why Do We Need It?
Creating some objects is expensive:
Database connections
Thread objects
Socket connections
Large memory objects
Repeated creation & destruction:
Slows performance
Increases GC pressure
Consumes resources
Object Pool:
Reuses objects
Improves performance
Controls max object count